# Test: interface backend vpp refuses policy routing.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse `policy route` under `interface
#           backend vpp` (even when `firewall backend vpp` matches), naming
#           `policy route` and `set interface backend kernel`?
#           A unit test cannot prove `policy-routes`'s registration reaches
#           `ze config validate` through the composition root.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-5 (policy routing) -- policy
#            routing programs Linux kernel ip rules and nftables marks, so it
#            is refused under VPP.
# PREVENTS: policy-based routing rules going into Linux kernel tables while VPP
#           forwards packets.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
firewall {
	backend vpp;
}
policy {
	route R {
		interface "eth*";
		rule block-quic {
			from {
				destination-port 443;
				protocol udp;
			}
			then {
				drop;
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=policy route
expect=stdout:contains=set interface backend kernel
